{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1521","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C. Nastia and a Hidden Permutation"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"3 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"This is an interactive problem!"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Nastia has a hidden permutation $$$p$$$ of length $$$n$$$ consisting of integers from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$. You, for some reason, want to figure out the permutation. To do that, you can give her an integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 2$$$), two "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"different"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" indices $$$i$$$ and $$$j$$$ ($$$1 \\le i, j \\le n$$$, $$$i \\neq j$$$), and an integer $$$x$$$ ($$$1 \\le x \\le n - 1$$$). "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Depending on $$$t$$$, she will answer: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$t = 1$$$: $$$\\max{(\\min{(x, p_i)}, \\min{(x + 1, p_j)})}$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$t = 2$$$: $$$\\min{(\\max{(x, p_i)}, \\max{(x + 1, p_j)})}$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You can ask Nastia "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"at most"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\lfloor \\frac {3 \\cdot n} { 2} \\rfloor + 30$$$ times. It is guaranteed that she will "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"not"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" change her permutation depending on your queries. Can you guess the permutation?"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The input consists of several test cases. In the beginning, you receive the integer $$$T$$$ ($$$1 \\le T \\le 10\\,000$$$) — the number of test cases."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"At the beginning of each test case, you receive an integer $$$n$$$ ($$$3 \\le n \\le 10^4$$$) — the length of the permutation $$$p$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It's guaranteed that the permutation is fixed beforehand and that the sum of $$$n$$$ in one test doesn't exceed $$$2 \\cdot 10^4$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"custom","title":"Interaction"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Interaction"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"To ask a question, print \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$t$$$ $$$i$$$ $$$j$$$ $$$x$$$\" ($$$t = 1$$$ or $$$t = 2$$$, $$$1 \\le i, j \\le n$$$, $$$i \\neq j$$$, $$$1 \\le x \\le n - 1$$$) Then, you should read the answer."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If we answer with $$$−1$$$ instead of a valid answer, that means you exceeded the number of queries or made an invalid query. Exit immediately after receiving $$$−1$$$ and you will see the Wrong Answer verdict. Otherwise, you can get an arbitrary verdict because your solution will continue to read from a closed stream."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"To print the answer, print \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"!"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$p_1$$$ $$$p_2$$$ $$$\\ldots$$$ $$$p_{n}$$$ (without quotes). "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note that answering doesn't count as one of the $$$\\lfloor \\frac {3 \\cdot n} {2} \\rfloor + 30$$$ queries"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"After printing a query or printing the answer, do not forget to output end of line and flush the output. Otherwise, you will get "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Idleness limit exceeded"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". To do this, use:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"fflush(stdout)"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" or "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cout.flush()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" in C++; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"System.out.flush()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" in Java; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"flush(output)"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" in Pascal; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"stdout.flush()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" in Python; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" See the documentation for other languages. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Hacks"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"To hack the solution, use the following test format."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line should contain a single integer $$$T$$$ ($$$1 \\le T \\le 10\\,000$$$) — the number of test cases."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case in the first line print a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$3 \\le n \\le 10^4$$$) — the length of the hidden permutation $$$p$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second line print $$$n$$$ space-separated integers $$$p_1, p_2, \\ldots, p_n$$$ ($$$1 \\le p_i \\le n$$$), where $$$p$$$ is permutation."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note that the sum of $$$n$$$ over all test cases should not exceed $$$2 \\cdot 10^4$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2\n4\n\n3\n\n2\n\n5\n\n3"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n? 2 4 1 3\n\n? 1 2 4 2\n\n! 3 1 4 2\n\n? 2 3 4 2\n\n! 2 5 3 4 1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Consider the first test case."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The hidden permutation is $$$[3, 1, 4, 2]$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"We print: \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$2$$$ $$$4$$$ $$$1$$$ $$$3$$$\" and get back $$$\\min{(\\max{(3, p_4}), \\max{(4, p_1)})} = 3$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"We print: \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$1$$$ $$$2$$$ $$$4$$$ $$$2$$$\" and get back $$$\\max{(\\min{(2, p_2)}, \\min{(3, p_4)})} = 2$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Consider the second test case."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The hidden permutation is $$$[2, 5, 3, 4, 1]$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"We print: \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$2$$$ $$$3$$$ $$$4$$$ $$$2$$$\" and get back $$$\\min{(\\max{(2, p_3}), \\max{(3, p_4)})} = 3$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"C","problemCode":"1521C","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1521/problem/C"}